signal — provenance note
=========================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling `bip340`/
`adaptor`/`frost`/`bolt8`/`dtls`/`falcon`/`slhdsa`/`oscore`/`spake2plus`
modules — self-contained protocol/crypto modules not folded into the root
`NOTICE`).

Provenance
----------

signal — clean-room implementation of the Signal Protocol's X3DH
(Extended Triple Diffie-Hellman) key-agreement and XEdDSA signature
scheme, specified in two public documents published by the Signal
Foundation / Trevor Perrin:

  - X3DH: "The X3DH Key Agreement Protocol", https://signal.org/docs/specifications/x3dh/
  - XEdDSA: "The XEdDSA and VXEdDSA Signature Schemes", https://signal.org/docs/specifications/xeddsa/

Both are public specifications — a public spec's text is not copyrightable
expression (merger doctrine, CONVENTIONS.md §5); implementing it, however
closely, is not "derived from" any third party's code. This module's
scaffold pass (`x3dh.zig`'s DH+HKDF composition and wire codecs,
`xeddsa.zig`'s doc comments describing the sign/verify construction) was
built directly from the two specification texts above — no third-party
X3DH/XEdDSA implementation (libsignal, in any of its C/Java/Rust/Swift
incarnations; Signal's own Axolotl-era code; any other language's port)
was read, ported, or consulted as a design reference for the Zig code,
types, or API shape, and the later XEdDSA implementation pass filled the
already-transcribed construction in unchanged (its ONLY libsignal
consultation was test-vector sourcing and variant identification — see
"Test vectors" below). Every construction detail in `xeddsa.zig`'s doc
comments (the sign-0 point-forcing convention, the `hash1`-vs-`hash`
domain separation, the four-DH `F || DH1..DH4` framing, the HKDF
salt/info shape) was drawn from the specification text itself.

`std.crypto.dh.X25519` / `std.crypto.ecc.Edwards25519` / `std.crypto.hash.
sha2.Sha512` / `std.crypto.kdf.hkdf.HkdfSha256` (all MIT, part of Zig
itself) supply the DH, curve, hash, and KDF primitives via their public
APIs; no new DH function, curve arithmetic, hash, or KDF primitive is
implemented here — the specifications' OWN composition of them (the
four-DH agreement, the Montgomery<->Edwards signature scheme) is this
module's contribution, and the two Signal specifications are the sole
references (no NOTICE-triggering third-party design reference exists for
this pass — CONVENTIONS.md §5's "pure clean-room from spec, no NOTICE
entry strictly required" case; this file is kept anyway per this
repository's established practice of a module-local NOTICE for
self-contained protocol/crypto modules, mirroring `oscore`'s precedent).

No GPL/LGPL/AGPL source was consulted or copied anywhere in this module.

Test vectors
------------

Neither the X3DH nor the XEdDSA specification text publishes a numeric
worked example (unlike, e.g., RFC 9383's Appendix C for SPAKE2+). The
X3DH agreement is therefore covered by a SELF-CONSISTENCY harness in
`src/kat_test.zig` (Alice's `initiateUnverified` and Bob's `respond`
must land on the identical `SK`/`AD` from independently-derived DH
computations — a property that would fail loudly on almost any
construction bug, even without an external oracle).

For XEdDSA, `src/kat_test.zig` embeds the known-answer vector from
libsignal's own test suite (`test_curve25519_signature` in
libsignal-protocol-c's `tests/test_curve25519.c`, GPLv3; the identical
bytes ship in libsignal-protocol-java): one private key, its public key,
one 33-byte message, and one 64-byte signature. These are NUMERIC FACTS
(a keypair and a signature over a fixed message), not copyrightable
expression — no libsignal code was ported, copied, or adapted. During
the XEdDSA implementation pass, libsignal's Rust `curve25519.rs`
(AGPL-3.0) and the C test file above were READ solely to (a) source that
vector and (b) establish the FACT — stated verbatim in the Rust file's
own doc comment — that deployed libsignal deviates from the XEdDSA paper
by carrying the signer's Edwards sign bit in the top bit of `s` instead
of forcing sign 0. This module's implementation itself was written from
the specification text (already fully transcribed into `xeddsa.zig`'s
doc comments during the scaffold pass, before any libsignal source was
looked at) and implements the PAPER's convention, deliberately NOT the
deployed variant — see `xeddsa.zig`'s module doc comment and `SPEC.md`.
`sign` is additionally cross-checked against `std.crypto.sign.Ed25519`'s
independent verifier (MIT, part of Zig).

Status of this pass
--------------------

**Part 1 complete.** `x3dh.zig`'s four-DH + HKDF agreement
(`initiateUnverified`/`respond`), both wire codecs (`PreKeyBundle`,
`InitialMessage`), the fail-closed `initiate`/`generateSignedPreKey`
entry points, and `xeddsa.zig`'s `sign`/`verify` (including
